<urn:atm:triage:finding/EQ-017>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "EQ-017" ;
  triage:title "CLI command-error log events carry error_code but drop the failure text -- message is always null" ;
  triage:description "fenix, 2026-09-15, colima container evidence (v1.5.20 closeout). A CLI command error writes a retained log event with \"message\": null even though a real error occurred. Example: /root/.atm/logs/atm.log.jsonl at 2026-09-15T03:42:28.497Z -- level Error, target atm.command, fields.code ATM_MESSAGE_VALIDATION_FAILED, message null. The CLI stderr for the same failure was 'invalid message id: localhost' (crates/atm-core/src/read/request.rs:162). Root-caused (team-lead, 2026-09-15): crates/atm/src/main.rs::map_command_event (line 686) hardcodes `message: None` on the LogEvent unconditionally, and build_command_event_fields (lines 647-659) only copies `event.command` and `event.error_code` into the fields map -- `event.error_message` (populated correctly upstream by CliObservability::report_fatal_error / retained_error_message in crates/atm/src/observability.rs) is never copied anywhere, so the failure text is silently dropped between CommandEvent construction and the persisted LogEvent. This is the same authoritative-log rule as EQ-016 (Rand, 2026-09-14: the log must carry the failure text) but a distinct code path -- EQ-016 fixed only the storage-side bounded mailbox reader lane; this is the CLI-side ScObservabilityAdapter command-error event mapping in atm/src/main.rs, unaffected by that fix." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "evidence_verification" ;
  triage:category "correctness" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:source "fenix, colima container evidence, atm 1.5.20, relayed 2026-09-15 (ATM message 01M2HKQQT17V2G1HW3EKEYTS4T); root-caused by team-lead same day" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm/src/main.rs::map_command_event and build_command_event_fields -- copy event.error_message into the LogEvent (either the top-level `message` field or a `fields[\"message\"]` entry) whenever it is Some, matching the authoritative-error-and-failure-evidence rule. Check for the same drop pattern anywhere else a CommandEvent's error_message is mapped into a persisted LogEvent outside this one CLI adapter." ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-15T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BB8 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-15T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/EQ-017/1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" ;
  triage:fixNote "cipher fixed (fix/eq-017-command-error-message @ 6691c6aca): map_command_event now sets message: event.error_message instead of hardcoding None, plus a real CLI integration test (crates/atm/tests/command_error_log.rs) reproducing 'atm ack localhost received' and asserting the persisted LogEvent.message carries the failure text. cipher's own just lint (38 checks) and just test (exit 0) passed pre-push. Lead-accepted (verdict posted on PR #1522 by fenix): just lint 38 checks passed, just test exit 0 including the new regression test. CI green (Test macos/ubuntu/windows-latest, Clippy, Format, all wheel builds, abi3 compatibility). Merged to develop at 574300fd6e554adb183b4b2da2e8c9fd52a60af9." .

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/EQ-017/1>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "crates/atm/src/main.rs" ;
  triage:line 686 ;
  triage:snippet "message: None, -- hardcoded in map_command_event; build_command_event_fields (line 647) never inserts event.error_message into fields either. Evidence: /root/.atm/logs/atm.log.jsonl @ 2026-09-15T03:42:28.497Z, level Error, target atm.command, fields.code ATM_MESSAGE_VALIDATION_FAILED, message null; CLI stderr for same failure was 'invalid message id: localhost'." ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:branch "develop" ;
  triage:headSha "574300fd6" ;
  triage:occursIn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/EQ-017/1> .

